_reason":"Closest volume per atom to the experimental reference (COD 7221359) among DFT structures in the experimental space group.","description":{"text":"CaZn2Sb2 crystallizes in the trigonal P-3m1 space group. Ca(1) is bonded to six equivalent Sb(1) atoms to form CaSb6 octahedra that share corners with twelve equivalent Zn(1)Sb4 tetrahedra, edges with six equivalent Ca(1)Sb6 octahedra, and edges with six equivalent Zn(1)Sb4 tetrahedra. All Ca(1)-Sb(1) bond lengths are 3.22 Å. Zn(1) is bonded to four equivalent Sb(1) atoms to form ZnSb4 tetrahedra that share corners with six equivalent Ca(1)Sb6 octahedra, corners with six equivalent Zn(1)Sb4 tetrahedra, edges with three equivalent Ca(1)Sb6 octahedra, and edges with three equivalent Zn(1)Sb4 tetrahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 20-53°. There are three shorter (2.69 Å) and one longer (2.80 Å) Zn(1)-Sb(1) bond length. Sb(1) is bonded to three equivalent Ca(1) and four equivalent Zn(1) atoms to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing SbCa3Zn4 pentagonal bipyramids.","dimensionality":3,"mineral":null,"mineral_distance":-1,"tool":"robocrystallographer","doi":"10.1557/mrc.2019.94"},"polyhedra":{"types":[],"sites":[{"label":"Ca1","element":"Ca","wyckoff":"1a","site_symmetry":"-3m.","oxidation_state":2.0,"cn":0,"ligands":"","shape":"none","polyhedron":false,"reason":"no ligands found"},{"label":"Zn1","element":"Zn","wyckoff":"2d","site_symmetry":"3m.","oxidation_state":2.0,"cn":0,"ligands":"","shape":"none","polyhedron":false,"reason":"no ligands found"},{"label":"Sb1","element":"Sb","wyckoff":"2d","site_symmetry":"3m.","oxidation_state":-3.0,"cn":0,"ligands":"","shape":"none","polyhedron":false,"reason":"no ligands found"}],"crystal_chemistry":{"pauling_rule_1_radius_ratio":[],"pauling_rule_2_electrostatic_valence":[],"pauling_rule_3_polyhedron_sharing":{},"pauling_rule_4_high_valence_sharing":[],"pauling_rule_5_parsimony":{},"bond_valence_sums":[],"global_instability_index":null,"b